{% alert level="info" %}
**Scroll anchoring (not in Astro yet)**: On Hugo content pages, the page scrolls to keep the selected tab button in the same position on the screen when the panel height changes. The API docs tabs in Hugo do not do this.
{% /alert %}

### Synced tabs

These two groups have the same labels. Select a tab in one group.

{% tabs %}
{% tab label="Linux" %}
Linux instructions for the first group.
{% /tab %}
{% tab label="Windows" %}
Windows instructions for the first group.
{% /tab %}
{% tab label="macOS" %}
macOS instructions for the first group.
{% /tab %}
{% /tabs %}

Text between the two groups.

{% tabs %}
{% tab label="Linux" %}
Linux instructions for the second group.
{% /tab %}
{% tab label="Windows" %}
Windows instructions for the second group.
{% /tab %}
{% tab label="macOS" %}
macOS instructions for the second group.
{% /tab %}
{% /tabs %}

{% alert level="info" %}
**Synced tabs (not in Astro yet)**: On Hugo content pages, when you select a tab, all groups on the page with the same label change to that tab.
{% /alert %}

{% alert level="info" %}
**URL persistence (not in Astro yet)**: On Hugo content pages, the selected tab goes into the `?tab=` query parameter. When the page loads, it opens that tab. If the URL also has an anchor, the page opens the tab and then scrolls to the anchor. In the Hugo API docs, the selected code example language goes into the `?code-lang=` query parameter and a `code-lang` cookie, and stays the same across pages.
{% /alert %}

{% alert level="info" %}
**Fallback to curl (not in Astro yet)**: In the Hugo API docs, all code examples on the page change to the language that you select. If an operation has no example in that language, its code example shows curl.
{% /alert %}

## Content found in API docs tabs

The API docs nest their content inside tabs. The examples below cover each type of content that the API spec puts inside a tab panel.

### Headings and inline formatting

{% tabs %}
{% tab label="Headings" %}
#### Metric alert query

Example: `time_aggr(time_window):space_aggr:metric{tags} [by {key}] operator #`

##### Query parameters

The query uses a time aggregation and a space aggregation.
{% /tab %}
{% tab label="Inline" %}
This endpoint requires **all** of the following permissions: `monitors_write` and `monitors_read`. The value is *optional* and defaults to `false`. For more information, see [Rate limits](/api/latest/rate-limits/).
{% /tab %}
{% /tabs %}

### Lists

{% tabs %}
{% tab label="Unordered" %}
This endpoint requires any of the following permissions:

- `user_access_manage`
- `user_app_keys`
- `service_account_write`
{% /tab %}
{% tab label="Ordered" %}
The upgrade process:

1. Identifies all hosts that match the filter query.
2. Validates that the specified version is available.
3. Begins to roll out the package upgrade to the target hosts.
{% /tab %}
{% /tabs %}

### Table

{% tabs %}
{% tab label="Table" %}
The following resource types support restriction policies:

| Resource type | Supported relations |
|---------------|---------------------|
| Dashboards | `viewer`, `editor` |
| Notebooks | `viewer`, `editor` |
| Powerpacks | `viewer`, `editor` |
| Service Level Objectives | `viewer`, `editor` |
{% /tab %}
{% tab label="Text" %}
A tab with plain text, next to a tab with a table.
{% /tab %}
{% /tabs %}

### Code block and alert

{% tabs %}
{% tab label="Code block" %}
The response has the following structure:

```json
{
  "data": [...],
  "meta": {
    "page": { "after": "..." }
  }
}
```

Use the `after` value to request the next page.
{% /tab %}
{% tab label="Alert" %}
{% alert level="warning" %}
**Note**: This endpoint is in preview and is subject to change. If you have any feedback, contact [Datadog support](/help/).
{% /alert %}

Get the list of annotation queue interactions.
{% /tab %}
{% /tabs %}

